       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. Doses that high carry a real risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the standard starting dose. It can be titrated to 10 mg.\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail or elderly patient or one with hepatic impairment. That doesn't apply to this patient.\n\nIf you do want 30 mg, I can enter it with a note recording that the dose is intentional. Tell me the clinical rationale, and I'll enter it that way. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
